# AHS advisory inference — environment template.
# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in real values. NEVER commit .env.
#
# OpenRouter API key. Used only by the remote advisory provider:
#   python -m harness.security_model --provider openrouter --allow-egress \
#       --model VENDOR/MODEL --prompt FILE --out NEW_FILE
# It is read from the process environment at runtime and is never written to the
# repo, the request URL, or the run receipt. Create one at
# https://openrouter.ai/keys  (key format: sk-or-v1-...).
#
# Load it into your shell before running (POSIX / WSL / macOS):
#   set -a; . ./.env; set +a
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Bring-your-own OpenAI-compatible router (e.g. a self-hosted NovaRouter / LiteLLM),
# used by:  python -m harness.security_model --provider custom [--allow-egress] ...
# AHS_ROUTER_URL is the full chat-completions URL of your router. A loopback URL
# (http://127.0.0.1:...) stays on-machine and needs no key; a remote one must be
# https, requires --allow-egress, and requires AHS_ROUTER_API_KEY. Example:
#   AHS_ROUTER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000/v1/chat/completions
AHS_ROUTER_URL=
AHS_ROUTER_API_KEY=
